            "map_preserves_multiplicity",
            "both_may_grow_with_keys"
          ]
        },
        "scoringContract": {
          "type": "choice",
          "resultSemantics": "exact_selected_set_with_partial_v1"
        },
        "feedback": {
          "reason": "Presence and multiplicity are different information contracts, while both structures may scale with distinct keys.",
          "details": "A set stores membership. A frequency map stores membership plus a count. Choosing between them should follow the information required by the result, not an assumption that one is always constant-space.",
