              "text": "Compare the real access model; a sequential scan may beat logarithmically many expensive random accesses."
            },
            {
              "id": "binary_always",
              "text": "Binary search is always faster because it makes fewer comparisons."
            },
            {
              "id": "scan_always",
              "text": "Scanning is always faster on remote data."
            },
            {
              "id": "ignore_latency",
              "text": "Use asymptotic classes without considering operation costs."
            }
