      {
        "id": "alg-ctpsw-slam-01",
        "prompt": "For nonnegative values, an algorithm seeks the longest contiguous segment with sum at most B. Why is “while sum > B, remove a[left] and increment left” a legal repair rule?",
        "interaction": {
          "type": "choice",
          "selectionMode": "single",
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "nonnegative_monotonicity",
              "text": "Removing a nonnegative value cannot increase the sum, so each shrink moves the window toward or into validity."
            },
            {
              "id": "two_indices",
              "text": "The rule is legal because left and right both move."
