          "details": "The transformation is a proof device: one BFS from a super-source reaches every real source at distance one, then reaches any vertex at one plus its minimum distance to the source set. Direct multi-source initialization removes the artificial offset and avoids materializing the extra vertex. Do not physically merge sources, because their identities and incident edges remain distinct.",
