          "details": "Under the BST invariant, inorder is the sorted sequence. The counter is therefore an index into that sequence and must advance exactly when a real node is emitted. Incrementing before the left call produces preorder ranks; incrementing after the right call produces postorder ranks. Null calls represent empty subtrees and add no element. Early termination is safe once the `k`th emission occurs because no later node can precede it in the inorder sequence.",
