        "scoringContract": {
          "type": "choice",
          "resultSemantics": "exact_selected_set_with_partial_v1"
        },
        "feedback": {
          "reason": "The terminal singleton is derivable from i, so an empty-state flag adds no information and violates minimality.",
          "details": "Base cases correspond to atomic instances of the declared subproblem, not universally to empty inputs. Here every legal state denotes a non-empty suffix. The state i == len(a) - 1 identifies a singleton suffix, whose answer is already known. Because terminal status and the final value are derivable from i and the shared array, neither an empty flag nor a saved last value belongs in minimal state. The transfer rule is to define the valid recursive domain first: if emptiness is outside that domain, do not add state merely to manufacture an empty terminal case.",
