          "reason": "The index alone distinguishes every remaining suffix; all other required information is fixed or derivable.",
          "details": "Recursive state should contain the information that changes the meaning of the current subproblem and cannot be reconstructed from stable context. Because a is immutable and shared, i uniquely identifies a[i:]. The child state is i + 1, and len(a) is derivable from a. A running total belongs to a different accumulator-style contract, while a copied suffix represents the same state less efficiently. This boundary transfers to any shared immutable sequence: use a position or interval when it uniquely identifies the remaining region; carry extra data only when the answer truly depends on it and it is not derivable.",
