          "details": "The recurrence is T(n) = T(floor(n/2)) + T(ceil(n/2)) + O(1). Across any level, the subranges partition the n elements, and the full binary recursion tree has n leaves and fewer than n internal nodes. Therefore total work is O(n), while maximum stack depth is O(log n) for balanced splits. The combiner max is valid because the parent maximum is one of the child maxima. This item counters the exponential-recursion heuristic without moving the primary target away from combining complete disjoint results.",
