      {
        "id": "recursion-basics-recursion-mistake-review-merge-sort-empty-only-base-self-range",
        "prompt": "A half-open recursive sort uses:\n\n    sort(lo, hi):\n        if lo == hi: return\n        mid = lo + (hi - lo) // 2\n        sort(lo, mid)\n        sort(mid, hi)\n        merge(lo, mid, hi)\n\nWhat happens on a one-element range hi - lo == 1?",
        "constraints": [
          "Ranges are half-open.",
          "mid uses floor integer division.",
          "The sort must support one-element ranges."
        ],
