          "details": "The reference supplies executable expected behaviour for inputs small enough to handle, while the invariant explains why the optimized state summarizes the same necessary information. Differential testing can expose boundary, duplicate, and update-order errors that examples omit; the proof guards against merely failing to sample a counterexample. A benchmark measures cost only after correctness is established. The transfer rule is to preserve an independent oracle whenever optimization compresses state, skips work, reorders operations, or introduces amortization.",
