          "details": "Constraints become useful only after they are translated into an approximate operation budget. For n = 200,000, O(n²) work is about 40 billion pair interactions, while O(n log n) and expected O(n) candidates remain in a plausible range. The numeric type does not erase the number of operations, and examples do not replace worst-case constraints. The transfer rule is to convert maximum sizes, query counts, and update counts into the dominant number of primitive operations before generating or ranking approaches.",
