        "feedback": {
          "reason": "The static prefix state is reusable across all one million queries. Its O(n) setup is amortized while per-query work drops to O(1).",
          "details": "For repeated static range sums, the complete models are O(n + q) time and O(n) extra space for prefix sums versus up to O(nq) time and O(1) extra space for rescanning. The array does not change, so the index remains valid, and the query operation is algebraically recoverable from two prefix values. Sorting neither preserves positional ranges nor needs to be repeated. The transfer rule is to invest in reusable preprocessing when the same data supports many compatible queries and the index remains valid for their entire lifetime.",
          "wrongOptionExplanationsByOptionId": {
