          "details": "Two timelines matter: when the data becomes available and when each answer is due. Here the dataset can be indexed during startup, and that index remains valid while unknown future queries arrive. The system cannot precompute each exact answer because query parameters are unknown, but it can precompute reusable structure such as a set, sorted copy, or prefix aggregates. Rebuilding per request would throw away the amortization benefit. The transfer rule is to separate data-offline/query-online workloads from true streaming-data workloads.",
