          "details": "The original prefix-sum rule relied on two facts: the data snapshot stayed stable, and the aggregate could be isolated by subtracting cumulative totals. Here almost every update makes a static prefix array stale, and median has no subtraction operation that removes an earlier prefix while retaining order statistics. Many queries increase the value of some reusable structure, but not this insufficient representation. The transfer rule is to re-check output, update model, state sufficiency, and invariant even when the new prompt uses familiar nouns.",
