              "maxPoints": 2
            },
            "feedback": {
              "reason": "There are RC states, each checks only a constant number of moves, and visited/frontier can each scale with the state count.",
              "details": "The implicit grid graph has V = RC and E = O(RC) under bounded-degree movement. Processing every state and four direction checks gives O(RC) time. A separate visited grid is O(RC), and the frontier can also contain O(RC) cells in the worst case. In-place marking can reduce the separate visited allocation, but it does not change traversal time and requires a mutation-safe contract."
