              "details": "In bottom-up heapify, most nodes are near the leaves and can move only a few levels; summing their possible work yields O(n), not n times the full height. Repeated insertion grows the heap incrementally, and the worst-case sum of logarithmic insertion heights is O(n log n). The methods produce the same heap contract but have different construction cost when all input is available in advance."
