              "details": "A good boundary test isolates the decision boundary with minimal unrelated structure. [1, 3) and [3, 5) share endpoint coordinates but no occupied instant under [start, end). The strict predicate returns false; the inclusive bug returns true. Clear overlap and clear separation exercise ordinary cases where both implementations agree. The same testing principle applies to event ties, insertion loop conditions, and merge equality: include exact handoffs, zero-width inputs, containment, and maximal numeric endpoints.",
              "wrongOptionExplanationsByOptionId": {
                "clear_overlap": "Both '<' and '<=' correctly report this as overlap, so it cannot discriminate the comparator boundary.",
                "clear_gap": "Both predicates correctly report a gap, so the equality defect remains hidden."
