            "feedback": {
              "reason": "All three intervals coexist over [3, 5), so capacity is three even though an adjacent scan performs only two pair comparisons.",
              "details": "Maximum concurrency is a pointwise property. At any t in [3, 5), each interval contains t, giving an active set of size three. Counting adjacent overlaps in an ordered list measures comparisons, not occupancy. End sorting can support a heap's release order or a greedy selection proof, but it does not collapse simultaneous meetings. Correct algorithms maintain active end times or an event-prefix count so that every currently active interval contributes to the maximum.",
              "wrongOptionExplanationsByOptionId": {
