              "details": "Ordinary meeting-room counting is the special case in which every interval contributes +1 at its start and -1 at its end. With weighted demand, use +weight and -weight events or an equivalent active-state structure. The maximum prefix sum is the capacity requirement. At time 4 the first demand is removed before any start at 4 under half-open semantics. This transfer preserves the concurrency mechanism but changes the accumulated quantity; pair counts and maximum individual demand are both insufficient.",
              "wrongOptionExplanationsByOptionId": {
