              "details": "Creating events costs O(n), sorting 2n events costs O(2n log(2n)) = O(n log n), and the final scan costs O(n). The stored event list contains O(n) records. If coordinates come from a small bounded integer universe U, a counting or difference-array approach may achieve O(n + U) time and O(U) space, but that is a different precondition and representation. Sorting intervals by end does not reduce the need for chronological event order. The cost derivation follows the number of events and the sorting model, not interval lengths."
