            "feedback": {
              "reason": "The invariant already covers both boundaries: no processed nodes yields null, and reversing one null link leaves S as the only node and new head.",
              "details": "For an empty list, current is null initially, so the loop performs zero iterations and prev remains null. For S, the algorithm saves null, sets S.next to prev (null), moves prev to S, and terminates. No swap partner, dummy data node, or self-cycle is needed. The null stopping rule assumes an acyclic input.",
              "wrongOptionExplanationsByOptionId": {
                "dummy_and_null": "Reversal does not require adding a logical node, and the existing single node remains the result.",
                "error_both": "The algorithm is defined for lists of length zero and one without pairwise swapping.",
                "s_self_cycle": "A one-node acyclic list remains S -> null; a self-link changes the structure into a cycle."
