              "details": "A wrapper sentinel can hold the updated head uniformly, but it does not become one of the nodes whose relative order is reversed. Reversing from dummy would place implementation scaffolding inside the result chain. Beginning at head.next would instead lose the original head from the reversal. A public sentinel-based representation could define a different contract, but that is not the stated one.",
              "wrongOptionExplanationsByOptionId": {
