              "details": "Internal reversal produces D -> C -> B. The untouched prefix must enter at D, and B must exit to E. Keeping A.next at B would enter the segment at its new tail and miss D and C; setting D.next to E would discard the reversed interior. This is the boundary extension from full-list reversal, where there is no external predecessor and the suffix is null.",
