              "details": "The worst sequence of Euclidean remainders is attained by consecutive Fibonacci numbers: each step reduces the pair to the preceding pair, so the number of iterations is proportional to the number of digits, O(log min(a,b)). The loop stores a, b, and r, giving O(1) extra space under the fixed-width cost model. A recursive implementation would additionally use O(log min(a,b)) call-stack space, which is outside the stated iterative contract."
            },
