              "details": "The proper crossing test alone excludes touching and overlap. Zero orientations must therefore be paired with finite on-segment bounds, while collapsed segments need point-specific treatment before a line direction is assumed. Rejection is safe only after all declared closed-boundary cases are exhausted. This order transfers to robust geometry generally: validate object type, evaluate the generic predicate, then resolve each legal boundary explicitly."
