              "details": "Compute target-current=-340, then normalize it modulo 360 into [-180,180). Adding 360 gives +20, the shorter counterclockwise rotation. Taking the raw subtraction confuses coordinate representatives with the cyclic relation. At an exact 180-degree tie, the declared half-open convention chooses -180; another API could choose +180, but it must do so consistently.",
              "wrongOptionExplanationsByOptionId": {
