              "type": "complexity",
              "maxPoints": 2
            },
            "feedback": {
              "reason": "The harmonic contribution over prime multiples yields O(N log log N) marking work, and the table stores one state per integer.",
              "details": "For each prime p, the sieve marks about N/p multiples. Summing 1/p over primes up to N grows like log log N, giving O(N log log N) total work for the standard analysis. The boolean table covers N+1 indices, so extra space is O(N). A segmented sieve changes the working-memory boundary but not the basic factor-marking invariant."
            },
