              "details": "Both inclusive and exclusive prefixes can be built over arbitrary sequences, including negative and repeated values. The choice affects storage shape, recurrence, and query formula—not whether the values are sorted. Sorting may change the problem’s positional semantics but cannot determine the convention.",
              "wrongOptionExplanationsByOptionId": {
                "exclusive_only_sorted": "An exclusive prefix works on any order because it is defined by indices and addition, not monotonicity.",
                "inclusive_only_unsorted": "Inclusive prefixes also work on sorted or unsorted input. Value order is orthogonal to endpoint inclusion.",
                "window_decides_sort": "A moving window may consume a prefix helper, but it does not redefine the helper’s persistent boundary contract."
