            "id": "recursion-basics-combine-subproblem-results-balanced-tournament-max-linear-work",
            "prompt": "tournamentMax(lo, hi) splits a non-empty array range into two disjoint halves, recursively finds each half's\nmaximum, and returns max(leftMax, rightMax). Each one-element range is terminal. Which cost explanation is correct?",
            "constraints": [
              "Every split produces disjoint halves whose union is the parent range.",
              "Each one-element range is visited once.",
              "The max operation is constant time."
            ],
            "difficulty": "advanced",
            "interaction": {
              "type": "choice",
              "selectionMode": "single",
              "options": [
