              "details": "A progress proof evaluates state values in each frame. For integer n > 1, floor division by two produces an integer satisfying 0 <= n // 2 < n. The base handles n <= 1, so no infinite descending chain is possible. Reusing the name n is normal because every call solves the same kind of subproblem. This distinction matters in traces: compare values under an explicit measure, not variable names, source-code line numbers, or stack depth.",
              "wrongOptionExplanationsByOptionId": {
