              "details": "The call graph is a single path through n real nodes plus one terminal None call, so total call count and time are O(n). Because each parent must add one after its child returns, ordinary evaluation retains the entire chain of frames at maximum depth, giving O(n) extra stack space. No branch duplicates work, so exponential time is unsupported. The distinction also shows why replacing recursion with an iterative pointer walk can preserve O(n) time while reducing auxiliary control space to O(1)."
            },
