              "reason": "The pointer count is linear, but the total bound inherits the operation guarantee of the chosen frequency structure.",
              "details": "The algorithm performs O(n) state operations because each element enters and leaves at most once. With an ordinary hash map, those operations are commonly analyzed as expected O(1), yielding expected O(n) time. A balanced ordered map would instead give O(n log K), while a fixed-array alphabet can provide deterministic O(1) updates. Claiming unconditional worst-case linear time requires a data-structure contract that supports it. The nested loop alone does not cause quadratic work.",
