              "reason": "Siblings share only their parent prefix, so a child must leave the caller-owned state exactly as it found it.",
              "details": "The branch invariant is “state on entry represents the root-to-parent prefix; state after adding the current node represents root-to-current.” When the call returns, it must restore the entry state. Keeping the left update contaminates the right path, while resetting to zero discards ancestors. Nodes at the same depth can have different values and therefore different prefixes, so depth is not a sufficient key. Passing an immutable numeric value instead of mutating shared state satisfies the same isolation rule without an explicit undo.",
              "wrongOptionExplanationsByOptionId": {
