              "details": "A leaf is a real node with no children. In this tree, the only root-to-leaf path is `5 → 4`, whose sum is `9`, so target `5` must fail. Testing at the missing right child of the root incorrectly treats “no edge here” as a completed path and accepts the root prefix. Testing every prefix answers a different question: whether any root-to-node path matches. The endpoint contract must be stated before recursion because the same arithmetic can support different path queries.",
              "wrongOptionExplanationsByOptionId": {
