              "details": "Recursive preorder implicitly schedules the left call before the right call. An explicit LIFO stack reverses insertion order, so the later push must be the earlier visit. After emitting the parent, push right and then left; the left child is now on top, and its entire subtree is processed before the stored right child. Both push orders visit the same set of nodes, but they do not produce the same ordered traversal. With a FIFO queue, insertion order would be preserved rather than reversed.",
