              "The decoder cannot seek backward.",
              "Null markers are legal stream tokens."
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "alg-tree-choice-bst-sorted-scan",
            "prompt": "A valid binary search tree must be streamed in nondecreasing value order using `O(h)` traversal state and no separate sorting step.\nWhich traversal should be selected?",
            "interaction": {
              "type": "choice",
              "selectionMode": "single",
              "options": [
                {
                  "id": "inorder",
                  "text": "Inorder DFS."
                },
                {
                  "id": "preorder",
                  "text": "Preorder DFS."
                },
                {
                  "id": "postorder",
                  "text": "Postorder DFS."
                },
                {
                  "id": "level_order",
                  "text": "Level-order BFS."
                }
              ],
              "acceptedOptionIds": [
                "inorder"
              ]
            },
            "scoringContract": {
              "type": "choice",
              "resultSemantics": "exact_selected_set_with_partial_v1"
            },
            "feedback": {
              "reason": "The BST invariant places smaller values in the left subtree and larger values in the right subtree, so left-node-right traversal is the sorted scan.",
              "details": "Inorder turns the structural BST ordering into a nondecreasing stream and needs only the recursive or explicit stack of height `h`. Preorder and postorder preserve useful construction or completion orders but do not sort values. Level order groups by depth, which is unrelated to numeric rank. Without the BST precondition, none of these traversals guarantees sorted output and an explicit sort or another ordered structure would be required.",
              "wrongOptionExplanationsByOptionId": {
                "preorder": "Parent-first order is useful for prefix serialization and branch pruning, but a parent can precede smaller values in its left subtree.",
                "postorder": "Child-first order is useful for subtree aggregates and deletion, but it can emit a right-subtree value before its parent and therefore does not preserve numeric rank.",
                "level_order": "Shallowest-first order reflects depth, not the BST value relation. It is appropriate for per-level or nearest-depth objectives, not for a globally sorted value stream."
              }
            },
            "taxonomy": {
              "primarySkillAtomId": "choose_tree_traversal_order",
              "secondarySkillAtomIds": [],
              "learningStage": "pattern_mechanics",
              "patternVariantId": "dfs_inorder",
