                "space": {}
              },
              "maxPoints": 2
            },
            "scoringContract": {
              "type": "complexity",
              "maxPoints": 2
            },
            "feedback": {
              "reason": "The call contract creates one constant-work call per node, while simultaneous recursive frames follow one root-to-leaf chain of length at most `h`.",
              "details": "Summing constant local work over exactly `n` non-null calls gives `O(n)` time. The two child calls do not remain active as two full subtrees at once; depth-first execution completes one branch before the other, so the maximum number of live frames is the current path length, `O(h)`. On a balanced tree, `h = O(log n)`; on a skewed tree, `h = O(n)`. The result changes if the call contract revisits subtrees, copies path-sized state, or stores an explicit frontier, because those add work or memory not present in the stated contract."
            },
