              "details": "For unique value pairs or one-copy compaction, later equal occurrences may be redundant after one representative is processed. For index-pair enumeration or counting, those occurrences remain distinct evidence and must be preserved or aggregated. The pointer configuration does not answer this semantic question. A correctness argument must name what identity the result uses and the point at which the value class has been consumed.",
