              "reason": "The O(n log n) sorting phase dominates the O(n) pointer phase.",
              "details": "The full algorithm has two sequential costs: preprocessing and scanning. Their sum is O(n log n + n), which simplifies to O(n log n). Reporting only O(n) describes the scan after the ordering precondition has already been paid for. When the input is already sorted, or when one sort is amortized across many queries, the relevant cost model changes."
            },
