              "details": "Evaluating the predicate first establishes whether the iteration contributes output. A kept value is copied to the current write position, then write advances to describe the enlarged valid prefix. Finally read advances for every input value. Conceptually separating these steps prevents unconditional write movement and makes the invariant visible even if code combines increments syntactically."
