              "details": "When all values are accepted, write and read remain aligned, and each conceptual copy may be a self-assignment. The invariant still holds: the prefix contains all kept values seen so far. An implementation may optimize away self-copies, but it must not change the pointer meaning or returned length. Neither reversal nor sorting is part of the output contract.",
              "wrongOptionExplanationsByOptionId": {
