              "details": "write should count only values actually placed in the result. If it advances for a rejection, the next accepted value is written too far to the right, leaving invalid data inside the claimed prefix. The loop may still terminate in linear time, which makes this bug easy to miss through complexity inspection alone. Correctness depends on conditional movement, not on both pointers making progress together.",
