              "details": "Because the input is sorted, equal values form runs. The first value of a run is written, and later equal values are rejected while read continues. Comparing against the last written value ties the duplicate policy directly to the valid-prefix invariant. Looking only at the next unread value can mishandle the final element or choose the last rather than the first representative without a stated reason.",
