              "details": "The read/write method keeps accepted values in their original order and visits each input once. Sorting by the predicate groups values but may reorder accepted values unless a stable sort and suitable tie behavior are guaranteed, and even then its O(n log n) time is unnecessary. The fact that sorting could produce a partition does not make its preprocessing free. Choose the direct invariant that matches the actual output contract.",
