              "details": "write counts accepted values among read processed values, so it cannot be greater than read. If write equals read, the assignment is a harmless self-write; if write is smaller, the overwritten position belongs to the processed prefix and its old content is no longer needed. The unread suffix begins after read and remains intact. This inequality is the correctness argument behind in-place safety.",
